    "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Permutation Given Using Alternate Notation",
    "problem": "$P(45,0)=$",
    "worked_solution": "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\n$P(45,0)$ means the same thing as ${}_{45}{P}_{0}.$ Using the usual formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(45,0) & =\\frac{45!}{(45-0)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{45!}}{\\cancel{45!}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
